            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Move session/conversation data storage from orphan branches on `the-intern` into the new private [`the-intern-data`](https://github.com/TheDeepestSpace/the-intern-data) repo.\n\nToday this data lives entirely on `the-intern`'s own branches, never touching `main`:\n- `telegram` branch → `convo.md` (rolling Telegram conversation summary)\n- ~80 `summaries/<repo-slug>/<issue#>` branches → per-PR/issue session summaries (`manage-summaries.js`)\n- `pending-retries` branch → usage-limit retry queue state\n\n## Blocker (needs a human)\n- [x] Grant the `the-intern-bot` GitHub App access to `TheDeepestSpace/the-intern-data`. Checked via `/installation/repositories` — the App is currently only installed on `svsch`, `the-intern`, `the-intern-testing`. This can't be done via API with the installation token; needs an org owner in GitHub UI (Settings → Applications → the-intern-bot → Configure → repository access → add `the-intern-data`). Blocks real read/write testing of everything below.\n\n## 1. Dual-write / dual-read during transition\n- [x] Update `manage-summaries.js` (fetch + save) and `telegram-session.yml`'s convo.md read/commit step to write new session summaries and convo.md updates into `the-intern-data` instead of (or in addition to, for now) `the-intern`'s orphan branches.\n- [x] During the transition, when fetching prior context give the agent data from **both** repos (old branches on `the-intern` + anything already migrated to `the-intern-data`) so nothing looks like it \"disappeared\" mid-cutover.\n- [x] Open a PR for this piece specifically (see dispatched comment below).\n\n## 2. Copy existing data into the-intern-data\n- [x] Copy the `telegram` branch content (convo.md + README) into `the-intern-data`.\n- [x] Copy all ~80 `summaries/<repo-slug>/<issue#>` branches into `the-intern-data`, organized the same way (or reorganize if it makes browsing easier there).\n- [ ] Decide whether `pending-retries` moves too (it's live queue state, not a note/record — probably stays on `the-intern`, confirm).\n\n## 3. Do the copy via git history, no rewrite of `the-intern`'s master\n- [ ] Since none of this lives on `main`, this is branch-level copying (fetch each orphan branch, push to the new remote / replay commits) — no `git filter-repo` / history rewrite of `the-intern` needed anywhere. Confirm this holds once the actual migration script is written.\n\n## 4. Full cutover\n- [ ] Once `the-intern-data` is confirmed populated and working, stop reading/writing summary and convo `.md` files on the `the-intern` side entirely — `the-intern-data` becomes the sole source.\n- [ ] Clean up (or just leave, TBD) the old `telegram` / `summaries/*` branches on `the-intern` afterward.\n\n---\nTracking issue only — no code changes here. Item 1 is being kicked off as a dispatched session in a follow-up comment.\n",
